# grid.list — the sampled-agreement GRID (founder order 2026-10-14:
# "the mechanically checked Rust/Cryptol sampled-agreement grid").
# Canonical, deterministic, structured — not random. One line per cell
# base: "<recs> <rows>" hex bit-masks over one step's 16 attempt slots;
# the harness runs each line under BOTH policy flags (optIn false, true).
#   recs bit a = attempt a JOURNALED as admitted (E_STEP_ADMITTED)
#   rows bit a = attempt a has an EFFECT ROW in the ledger
# recs patterns cover: empty, single slots, contiguous admission prefixes
# (the shapes the run path itself generates), saturation (0xFFFF), the
# only-slot-15 and 0-and-15 corners, holes, and alternating masks.
# rows patterns cover: empty, each single low slot, slot 15 alone,
# contiguous prefixes, all-rows, mixed corners, alternating masks.
# SAMPLED AGREEMENT IS AN INTERMEDIATE GATE: it binds the twin's
# definitions to the Rust definitions over this grid — it is NOT SAW
# implementation correspondence and claims no exhaustiveness over the
# 2^33 input space.
